##
#
# Pressure perturbation over a 1D isothermal steady state proposed by
# LeVeque and Bale [1], in the configuration of [2], Section 4.1.4 (Figure
# 4.2) of [3].
#
# A small pressure perturbation is added to the isothermal equilibrium
#
#   rho_e = exp(-(x - 2)),  p_e = exp(-(x - 2)),  v = 0,
#
# such that the initial state is given by
#
#   p = p_e + eta exp(-100 (x - 2.5)^2),
#   theta = (1 / rho_e) * p^(1/gamma),
#
# with eta = 0.01. The perturbation splits into two acoustic waves
# travelling in opposite directions. The computational domain is [0,5] with
# slip boundary conditions. The thermodynamic constants are p_0 = 1,
# c_v = 2.5, gamma = 1.4 (thus R = 1) and g = 1.
#
# The chosen 200 subdivisions correspond to the coarsest mesh of Figure 4.2
# of [3]; the figure shows 200, 400, and 800 cells, as well as a reference
# solution. The final time is set to t = 0.8 and we output a vtk every
# δt = 0.008.
#
# The scheme preserves the isothermal equilibrium exactly, see
# 2026-FMT-4.1.4-isothermal_well_balanced.prm for the corresponding Table
# 4.4 of [3].
#
# [1] R. J. LeVeque, D. S. Bale. Wave propagation methods for conservation
#     laws with source terms. In: M. Fey, R. Jeltsch (eds.), Hyperbolic
#     Problems: Theory, Numerics, Applications, pp. 609-618, Birkhäuser,
#     1999. DOI 10.1007/978-3-0348-8724-3_12
#
# [2] A. Navas-Montilla, I. Echeverribar. A family of well-balanced WENO and
#     TENO schemes for atmospheric flows. J. Comput. Phys., 489:112273,
#     2023. DOI 10.1016/j.jcp.2023.112273
#
# [3] C. Farris, M. Maier, E. J. Tovar. Well-balanced second-order
#     approximation of the compressible atmospheric Euler equations.
#     Preprint, 2026. arXiv:2606.19764
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = pressure-perturbation
  set tasks             = vtu output
  set final time        = 0.8
  set timer granularity = 0.008
end

subsection B - Equation
  set dimension          = 1
  set equation           = euler atmospheric
  set c_v                = 2.5
  set gamma              = 1.4
  set gravity            = 1
  set reference pressure = 1
end

subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry        = rectangular domain
  set mesh refinement = 0

  subsection rectangular domain
    set position bottom left     = 0
    set position top right       = 5
    set subdivisions x           = 200
    set boundary condition left  = slip
    set boundary condition right = slip
  end
end

subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = function
  set position      = 0

  subsection function
    set density expression               = exp(-x+2)
    set velocity x expression            = 0
    set potential temperature expression = (1/exp(-x+2)) * (exp(-x+2)+0.01*exp(-100*(x-2.5)^2))^(1/1.4)
  end
end

subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min = 0.05
  set cfl max = 0.05
end

subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection full
    set vtu output quantities = p, schlieren_rho
  end
end
